  body: |
    # ESA third-party deductions and evidence of liability

    ## Authored interpretation

    The source describes discretion to pay deductions to third parties, requires liability for the debt and provides for evidence where liability is disputed.

    ## Scope and boundaries

    DMG 46131 and 46133–46138 retain claimant/partner distinctions: a partner’s or dependant’s fine is excluded by the cited note. Consent, limits, priority and the detailed scheme conditions remain unresolved; a bill alone is not an automated deduction decision.

    ## Inspected source passages

    - [DMG 46131, PDF page 28](https://assets.publishing.service.gov.uk/media/69e5ffc3de262afd82fcf92b/dmg-Chap-46.pdf#page=28)
    - [DMG 46133, PDF page 29](https://assets.publishing.service.gov.uk/media/69e5ffc3de262afd82fcf92b/dmg-Chap-46.pdf#page=29)
    - [DMG 46134, PDF page 29](https://assets.publishing.service.gov.uk/media/69e5ffc3de262afd82fcf92b/dmg-Chap-46.pdf#page=29)
    - [DMG 46136, PDF page 29](https://assets.publishing.service.gov.uk/media/69e5ffc3de262afd82fcf92b/dmg-Chap-46.pdf#page=29)
    - [DMG 46137, PDF page 29](https://assets.publishing.service.gov.uk/media/69e5ffc3de262afd82fcf92b/dmg-Chap-46.pdf#page=29)
    - [DMG 46138, PDF page 29](https://assets.publishing.service.gov.uk/media/69e5ffc3de262afd82fcf92b/dmg-Chap-46.pdf#page=29)

    ## Evidence and review status

    This is an unreviewed, model-assisted interpretation of selected passages in the frozen DWP guidance. It is an independent experimental publication, not an official DWP document, an entitlement decision or an executable benefits rule. ESA(Cont), ESA(IR), New Style ESA, UC and Pension Credit are not equated. The captured source contains historical, transitional and potentially superseded provisions; no complete or current legal rule set is claimed. Machine extraction can affect reading order, footnotes and characters. No visual PDF review or specialist acceptance is claimed.

